<p><strong>seeking to greenlight:</strong> yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP article</p>
<p><strong>Page layout:</strong> Audio log, Camera log MTF log</p>
<p><strong>Elevator pitch:</strong> This SCP is a Mongolian (Khun) teenage boy that can manipulate any natural structure and has the ability to create Giant creature that varies depending on the SCP's imagination, however its consistent manifestation is a Asian dragon. This SCP can look through any animal that it know inner workings of (anatomy) like wolf, eagle, hummingbirds and involves any type of farm animals</p>
<p>However, it can't manifest creatures if it's not touching dirt or not surrounded by any natural habitats, is incredibly sensitive to fire, bomb involving any heavy firearm.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Central&nbsp;Narrative</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Central&nbsp;Narrative</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> After mass death and disappearance of local cattle and destruction of major mining factory in Erdenet Rhashaat in Mongolia, The Foundation dispatched a research team to try to find out what this SCP is. they found out that this SCP is known among the locals as a fairy tale, folklore making it alive since the Khun era.</p>
<p>After a couple of days, one of the nearby mining factories exploded killing all of the workers!</p>
<p>Learning what this SCP does The Foundation dispatched an MTF Theta-4 (Gardeners) to contain it. but GOC and Chaos Insurgency also found out about this SCP which causes all of them to go on a wild goosed chase and competition for this SCP.</p>
<p>the GOC tried to kill it while Chaos insurgency tried to use it. the foundation or this MTF team is preventing it.<br />
They chase this SCP around until it get fed up with them and tries to kill them all! Which made The foundation and GOC team up to have it contained.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention:</strong> I'm basing the story on the SCP foundation motto. &quot;Protect&quot;. I like the idea that the SCP Foundation is in constant competition to contain the anomaly so that no one can use them in for their own gain or kill it.</p>
<p><strong>Note:</strong> this is my second SCP concept decided to put the other one in back burner.</p>

							</div>

								
					
