			<div class="content" id="post-content-4826840">
									

<blockquote>
<p>Then one test shows no results. Given that keyboard spam still gave results, what is the one thing that doesn't exist in any dimension?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>My concern here is like&#8230;any interesting thing here has to exist? I'm like, really unsure how 'there is one thing that doesn't exist anywhere' can be interesting because like&#8230;surely it has to exist enough for us to know what the implications of it not existing are?</p>
<p>Iunno, my concern is that you've built this big narrative around the foundation trying to find this one test out again with them devoting a lot of resources to it but I don't really have an idea of what the <em>stakes</em> of this are: like, if the Foundation finds the thing, what happens? Why is the answer so important?</p>
<p>On a higher level, AWCY? feel like a strange fit here? They do anart, and it feels like that's pretty far removed from 'writing a strange search engine'? But then, AWCY? have done computer based art before; it's more, the search engine doesn't really feel like an art piece over it being computer based, y'know?</p>

							</div>

								
					
