																	<a href="/forum/t-13872203/just-an-unordinary-camera#post-4826826">Re: Just an unordinary camera</a>
									</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/cybersqyd" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5336470); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5336470&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606225470" alt="cybersqyd" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5336470)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/cybersqyd" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5336470); return false;" >cybersqyd</a></span> <span class="odate time_1606211340 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">24 Nov 2020 09:49</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-89000/help:ideas-critique">Writing Help / Help: Ideas Critique</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13872203/just-an-unordinary-camera">Just an unordinary camera</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4826826">
									

<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;Open&nbsp;for&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>Once he realised that the date and picture are connected he handed it in for further investigation.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>So this is, for me, the point where the actual story in the article kicks off; before this is just&#8230;discovery stuff which is fine but it's not as interesting as exploring what the Foundation does with the camera and that leads me to the big question: what actually happens with this?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Alot of test logs of important historical events (e.g.: life of Jesus Christ) would be part of the article. Most of the importnat information would obviously be blacked out or would require O5 authorisation to access it.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Why are these test logs gonna be interesting to read? My concern is that you're just going to hint at there being interesting stuff here, which is a lot less interesting to read about than actually having interesting stuff; and I would <em>strongly</em> urge you to reconsider relying on heavy blackboxing here (see <a href="/avoid-the-blackbox">What Hides Beneath: the Black and White of Blackboxing</a> for a modern take on how to use redaction).</p>
<p>Beyond this, focusing on historical stuff feels like it's squandering the potential a little: it feels like this is a thing the foundation could use to predict future events and in turn, like something the foundation could be tricked by and accidentally cause something horrible to happen but??</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

